<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21400" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignĭo</span></b> , īvi or
			ĭi, ītum, 4, v. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to ignite</i>, <i>set on fire</i>, <i>make red-hot</i> (post-class.): ut igniverint,
			Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10,
			1077.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignītus</span></b> , a, um, P.
			a., <i>fiery</i>, <i>glowing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 6, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aether, App. de Mundo, p. 57: tela,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			 p. 61.— <i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod vinum natura esset ignitius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 8, 10</span></i>
			.—<i>Sup.</i>: draconis effigies
			ignitissima, Jul. Var. Rer. Gest. Alex. 3, 56.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 546</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 11</span></i>.</div>
